  <h2 id="cost">Total cost and time against your budget</h2>

  <p>
    Take the whole education budget your family can sensibly spend, including living costs, tools, books, internet, projects and
    future upskilling. As a strict starting heuristic, keep the course itself near 10% of it, and treat anything above about 20% as
    needing course-specific proof. These are planning limits, not facts of nature.
  </p>

  <div class="comparison-grid">
