  <h2 id="practice">The business layer: who pays and how they find you</h2>

  <p>
    A qualified CA, CS or CMA can run a practice, and that is where income can grow past a salary. ACCA, CFA and FRM are mostly employer
    routes, so the sales layer matters there for a side route or a later move. Here is the basic picture for the practice routes.
  </p>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--teal">
    <p>
      <strong>The scalable path.</strong> An independent CA, CS or CMA practice scales through repeat clients: GST and tax filings,
      audits, company compliance and cost reviews come back every cycle. You set your own fees, you can hire trained juniors, and one
      satisfied client refers the next. It takes years and a client base. It does not come from the letters alone.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="feature-grid">
    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-card__label">Who pays</div>
      <div class="feature-card__title">Small firms and family businesses</div>
      <p>Owners who need returns filed, books checked, company filings made or costs understood, and who would rather hand it to someone they trust.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-card__label">How they find you</div>
      <div class="feature-card__title">Referrals first</div>
      <p>A happy client, a banker, a lawyer or a former employer. Warm introductions beat cold outreach, and your training firm is often your first source.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-card__label">First skill to learn</div>
      <div class="feature-card__title">Position a niche and a fixed scope</div>
      <p>"GST compliance for small traders in my city" beats "all tax work". Describe a clear fixed scope in conversation, follow up, ask for referrals, and learn to talk about price calmly.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-card__label">One number to watch</div>
      <div class="feature-card__title">Enquiries that become paid work</div>
      <p>Count how many conversations turn into an engagement. If the number is low, the offer or the follow-up needs work, not more hours.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="honest-take">
    <p class="honest-take__label">Honest take: sell within the rules</p>
    <p>
      Professional bodies limit how members promote themselves. ICAI treats solicitation and advertising as restricted, and its 2020
      website advisory lists banned items such as stating fees, calling a firm "best" or "leading", client names or logos, rankings and
      "why choose us" pages. A 13th edition of the ethics code reportedly takes effect from 1 April 2026 with more flexibility, so read the
      current text before you build anything. Your growth tools are referrals, useful educational content and doing good work.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    Pay no one for "guaranteed clients". A fee-only SEBI adviser practice, a US-client accounting service under CPA rules, or a
    compliance desk for small firms are real models, and each has its own licence rules to follow first.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">What AI changes for accounting and compliance work</h2>

  <p>
    Be specific about the pressure. Matching entries, first-draft working papers, routine reconciliations and basic return preparation are
    the tasks tools already do. A June 2025 report said UK Big Four graduate intake fell by up to 29% at some firms over two years, with
    graduate accountancy adverts down 44%, and quoted a recruiter saying firms were looking at AI to replicate junior work. The same
    report said firms are expanding offshoring to India and building AI assurance services. We found no reliable India number for
    displaced fresher audit roles, so do not trust one you see in an advert.
  </p>

  <ol class="scorecard-list">
    <li class="scorecard-item">
      <span class="scorecard-item__circle">1</span>
      <div class="scorecard-item__body">
        <div class="scorecard-item__title">Now</div>
        <p>Use AI to draft formulas, explain a tax provision or first-pass a reconciliation. Verify every figure against the source document. Keep a note of what you checked.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="scorecard-item">
      <span class="scorecard-item__circle">2</span>
      <div class="scorecard-item__body">
        <div class="scorecard-item__title">Next</div>
        <p>Build one repeatable, checked workflow for a service you can sell, such as monthly compliance review for a small business. Learn data tools such as Excel and Power BI.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="scorecard-item">
      <span class="scorecard-item__circle">3</span>
      <div class="scorecard-item__body">
        <div class="scorecard-item__title">Later, as tools and adoption mature</div>
        <p>Value shifts to judgment, sign-off, advice and explaining numbers to an owner. Services such as assurance on AI systems may open, though no tool or credential guarantees that.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <p>
    The bodies are moving too. ICAI teaches IT and soft skills in a four-week course before training and offers a digital ecosystem
    and controls module in its Final options. ACCA's redesign from 2027 gives more weight to AI and technology and adds a data science
    option. Learning that layer early is a reasoned bet, not a promise.
  </p>

  <h2 id="abroad">Study-abroad caution for ACCA, CPA and CFA moves</h2>

  <p>
    An exam pass does not create a visa, a job or a licence. Check four things before you plan a move around one of these: whether the
    target country recognises the credential for the work you want, which regulator controls practice, what the licence needs beyond the
    exam, and how you will fund the gap.
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>The US CPA exam can be taken in India, so you do not need to study abroad to start. A US degree to reach 150 credit hours is the expensive route. Many states now accept 120 hours plus two years of experience, so check your state board first.</li>
    <li>ACCA is recognised in many places, but each country decides who may practise. Do not assume a recognition claim from an advert.</li>
    <li>CFA and FRM are exams plus work hours. A foreign degree is not part of the requirement.</li>
    <li>A large education loan that depends on a visa, a foreign job or an exchange rate is a high-risk commitment. Compare the debt-light route first, and read the guide on <a href="/blog/study-abroad/education-loan-for-study-abroad-india/">education loans for study abroad</a>.</li>
  </ul>

